{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_wind_earth_v",
    "description": "Rotate A-grid COVARIANT winds (ua,va) to EARTH-RELATIVE (meridional component) at each cell centre -- step 2 of the Mouallem 2023 vector halo remap. Physical velocity from the covariant components via the metric raise g^ij=(1/sin2A)[[1,-cosA],[-cosA,1]] with the node-tangent basis e1,e2 (e_i=normalize(cross(cross(ka,kother),ka)) from duo_cell_center), then dotted with the local meridional (elat) unit vector (elon=(-sinL,cosL,0) / elat=(-sinP cosL,-sinP sinL,cosP), lon=atan2, lat=asin from the cell centre). Earth-relative winds are globally continuous, so the halo is then filled by the scalar duo_extend and rotated back by duo_wind_cov_v. Params [ua,va,center]; bind center=duo_cell_center; R_sphere free name. Verified to ~3e-16 vs a direct reimplementation.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:wind_rotate",
      "order:0",
      "bc:duo",
      "axes:tile,x,y",
      "form:rotate",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Mouallem, J., Harris, L., & Chen, X. (2023). Implementation of the novel Duo-Grid in GFDL's FV3. JAMES, 15, e2023MS003712."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_wind_assy_13.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_wind_assy_14.esm"
    }
  ],
